From 9b6f10405864dca556e4c432c4adc7f02157cd88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:18:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): deliver alerts over the background connection

The background connection kept Paseo connected, but alerts still never
showed: on phones sendOsNotification is a no-op and every alert is a remote
push, which needs Google services that HarmonyOS's Android compatibility
layer does not have.

While the background connection runs, show agent and terminal alerts as
local notifications on an Agent alerts channel, routed on tap like a push.
Stop registering the push token for that time and revoke it, so a device
with Google services does not get each alert twice. Turning the switch on
now asks for notification permission first, since Android 13 hides the
service's notification and every alert without it, and says so when it is
denied.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
